# State and memory

- One **canonical structured** conversation state. Model prose is not source of truth.
- Important fields should carry: value, validation status, source, timestamp when relevant, confidence when inferred, persistence status when relevant.
- Distinguish: explicit user input | inferred | user-confirmed | backend-verified.
- Confirm low-confidence location/treatment before irreversible actions.
- Never overwrite a confirmed value with a weaker inference; do not re-ask already valid fields.
- State transitions must be explicit and testable.
- Do not mix agency, clinic, and patient state; enforce tenant/agency boundaries on reads and writes.
- Avoid unnecessary sensitive data in prompts/logs; prefer compact validated state over full chat dumps when sufficient.

Inspect the active surface’s state owner under `lib/agency/` or the relevant public chat route before changing state shape.
